                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'll be perfectly honest, I was enjoying this game up until the very last moment, when I accidentally started a new game and it cleared all my nature crystals.\n\nI didn't think anything of it at the time because I had loads of save files, and why would a new game affect those?\n\nBut I soon realised, yes, that accidental click destroyed all the saved choices I had already experienced, and so in order for me to get all the endings I would have to repeat all that repetitive dialogue and slow reminiscing scenes over and over again.\n\nSo now I'm kind of uncaring about it.\n\n________________________\n\n\nBefore this rotten disaster happened, I did manage to get ending 2, 3 and 4 out of 6. I think what makes this game unusual is that by selecting certain choices, you get gifted a 'nature crystal', with a total of 30 existing in the game. With no guide to go by, I thought it was going to be hard, but the game is relatively short so normally it wouldn't be a problem.\n\nExcept the game decided to delete all my crystals.\n\n\n__________\n\n\nStory-wise, it doesn't really satisfy. There are two characters besides the protagonist that are the main story, but in the pace of 3 days the story is over? With just one or two actual conversations? It kind of defies logic, or beggars belief at any rate. For such a short story, I don't recommend the game unless it is 80-90% off.",
